            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic image (345). A woman with abdominal pain and purulent vaginal discharge].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2271</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 41-year-old woman presented with abdominal pain and purulent vaginal discharge several months after a complicated laparoscopic cholecystectomy. MRI revealed a rectovaginal pouch abscess which at laparotomy contained 41 gallstones that had been spilled.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
